cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Whoosh (the whoosh3 distribution) in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Whoosh: a fast, pure-Python full-text indexing and search library"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Whoosh is a fast, featureful, pure-Python full-text indexing and search
  library. It was originally created by Matt Chaput, maintained for a time by
  the whoosh-community organization and later revived as whoosh-reloaded, and
  is now maintained under the whoosh3 distribution on PyPI with support for
  modern Python versions.
authors:
  - family-names: Chaput
    given-names: Matt
  - name: "Priya Sundaram"
  - name: "The Whoosh community and prior contributors"
license: BSD-2-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/priya-sundaram-dev/whoosh"
url: "https://priya-sundaram-dev.github.io/whoosh/"
keywords:
  - "full-text search"
  - "information retrieval"
  - "indexing"
  - "BM25"
  - "pure-python"
  - "search-engine"
